@startuml
title Public Transport Tracker - Backend Architecture

package "Frontend" {
  [React Web App] as WebApp
}

package "API Layer" {
  [TransportController] as TransportController
  [CacheController] as CacheController
}

package "Service Layer" {
  [TransportService] as TransportService
  [RoutePlannerService] as RoutePlannerService
  [AlertService] as AlertService
  [MockDataService] as MockDataService
  [CacheService] as CacheService
}

package "Client Layer" {
  interface TransitApiClient
  [MtaApiClient] as MtaApiClient
  [TransitLandApiClient] as TransitLandApiClient
  [SeptaApiClient] as SeptaApiClient
  [TflApiClient] as TflApiClient
}

database "In-Memory Cache\n(InMemoryCache)" as DB
cloud "External Transit Providers\n(MTA, TransitLand, TfL, SEPTA)" as External

WebApp --> TransportController : HTTP /api/v1/transport
WebApp --> CacheController : HTTP /api/v1/cache

TransportController --> TransportService : delegate
CacheController --> CacheService : diagnostics / invalidation

TransportService --> CacheService : get / put / getStale / withKeyLock
TransportService --> RoutePlannerService : plan()
TransportService --> AlertService : getServiceAlerts()
TransportService --> MockDataService : getMockData()
TransportService --> TransitApiClient : fetch...
TransitApiClient <|.. MtaApiClient
TransitApiClient <|.. TransitLandApiClient
TransitApiClient <|.. SeptaApiClient
TransitApiClient <|.. TflApiClient

CacheService --> DB : stores TransportData
MtaApiClient --> External : live API calls
TransitLandApiClient --> External : live API calls
SeptaApiClient --> External : live API calls
TflApiClient --> External : live API calls

note right of TransportService
  Resilience chain:
  OFFLINE → CACHE → LIVE → STALE_CACHE → MOCK
end note

@enduml
